==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
Portmanteau made of [[retro-]] and [[refit|(re)fit]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|retrofits|retrofitting|retrofitted|retrofitted}} (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')
# To [[add]] or [[substitute]] new [[part]]s or [[component]]s to some [[device]], [[structure]] etc., that were not previously [[available]]; to [[modernize]]
# To fix an older [[version]] (or older versions) as part of the same process of fixing the newest version
#:''The bug was so bad that we had to '''retrofit''' our patch to the last three releases, as well as the newest release.''

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
# Something that has been retrofitted
# The act of retrofitting

===Adjective===
'''retrofit'''
# of, relating to, or being a retrofit

